<article class="env-remark" id="0GIX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GIX">Remark <span data-tag="0GIX">59.53.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $K \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale})$. Let $\overline{s}$ be a geometric point of $S$. There are always canonical maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (Rf_*K)_{\overline{s}} \longrightarrow R\Gamma (X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}), p^{-1}K) \longrightarrow R\Gamma (X_{\overline{s}}, K|_{X_{\overline{s}}})  \]
</div>
  <p> where $p : X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}) \to X$ is the projection. Namely, consider the commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X_{\overline{s}} \ar[r] \ar[d]^{f_{\overline{s}}} &  X \times _ S \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}) \ar[r]_-p \ar[d]^{f'} &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  \overline{s} \ar[r]^-i &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}) \ar[r]^-j &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> We have the base change maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  i^{-1}Rf'_*(p^{-1}K) \to Rf_{\overline{s}, *}(K|_{X_{\overline{s}}}) \quad \text{and}\quad j^{-1}Rf_*K \to Rf'_*(p^{-1}K)  \]
</div>
  <p> (Cohomology on Sites, Remark <a href="/tag/07A7" data-tag="07A7">21.19.3</a>) for the two squares in this diagram. Taking global sections we obtain the desired maps. By Cohomology on Sites, Remark <a href="/tag/0E47" data-tag="0E47">21.19.5</a> the composition of these two maps is the usual (base change) map $(Rf_*K)_{\overline{s}} \to R\Gamma (X_{\overline{s}}, K|_{X_{\overline{s}}})$. </p>
</article>